    ":question/id": "66cc8550-5653-59d7-83fc-1ba0962c771f",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-54340",
    ":question/problem": "![](images/87/873c7f6b6e036f592f693bf2d20e1980b890f888d08af40b775cb77deba07a76.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the parallelogram $ABCD?$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The diagonal $\\overset{\u2015}{BD}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $\u25b3ABD$ (see the illustration).\n\n![](images/75/7572dac85d8e6029b52d199bdfcb87b4a92ffafc008fe999c10848153f9f67d8.png)\n\n Computing the area of $\u25b3ABD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(10)(6)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{38}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{38}^{\u2218} \\\\  & \u224818.470,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ABD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 18.470 \\\\  & =36.940.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $37.$"
  },
