    ":question/problem": "![](images/24/243e5fd1911db6fc7dc940a16082c7369c63f913d78d9e18324d977540a310cb.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The diagonal $\\overset{\u2015}{BD}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $\u25b3CBD$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/da/da5c25d9e1e54a79b8e2c8532d4571dd42ccd4e6e6a3fa69aa1fc9075c19b39d.png)\n\n Computing the area of $\u25b3CBD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{CBD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(21)(12)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{66}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =126\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{66}^{\u2218} \\\\  & \u2248115.107,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{CBD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 115.107 \\\\  & =230.214.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $230.$"
